From 4c3b32e6e3bc5a7ba1fbda4a841f58c209e5cdb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alaric McKenzie-Boone <alaric.mckenzie.boone@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:58:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] rewards: native exactly-once receipt + cargo-contest
 provider surface (#441)

Add the engine-free provider surface requested by lane 18 (#441/#220):

- pc_port/pc_p2_receipt.h: versioned ordinary/pod receipt vocabulary,
  exactly-once ReceiptLedger over a persistence backend, memory and durable
  atomic-file adapters, descriptor validation and ordinary/pod reconciliation
  that refuses a pod-only source covering an ordinary check.
- pc_port/pc_p2_cargo_contest.h: the agreed cargo-contest transition table
  (Held/Stolen/ReleasedToSource + release reason), carrier tokens instead of
  engine pointers (no dangling helper), cleared on release/death/interruption/
  revisit/reset, and an exactly-once receipt hook into the shared ledger.
- tools/p2_receipt_test.cpp and tools/p2_cargo_contest_test.cpp exercise
  replay/restart, corruption rejection, the ordinary/pod split and a
  small-Breadbug-style contest consumer.
